        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Europe</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of the Kalka River</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">31 May 1223; by another reckoning the main defeat came three days earlier and the fighting ended, at the Kievan camp, on 31 May</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Kalka River, now in Donetsk Oblast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>; the river's location is not known for certain, and it is thought to be the Kalchyk, which flows into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-azov">Sea of Azov</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">Rus' princes, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mstislav-mstislavich">Mstislav the Bold</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>, Mstislav III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> and Mstislav of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chernigov">Chernigov</a>, with no commander-in-chief, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumans">Cumans</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koten">Köten</a>, against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jebe">Jebe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subutai">Subutai</a>. Strengths are estimates: for the Rus' from 8,000 (Sverdrup) to 80,000 (Gabriel, Munro); for the Mongols 20,000 (de Hartog) or about 23,000 (Gabriel).</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> won. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumans">Cumans</a> and most of the Rus' hosts were routed, the Kievan camp surrendered after three days, and its princes were killed. The Mongols did not go on to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> and turned east.</span></div>
        </div>
